comments:
I am not aware of what kind of call does the TTS service to Volumio. If someone is able to provide an example call, we can make a workaround in Volumio to make that work (or fix the incompatibility for good).

@schnabel from your reply it seems that a string is passed while Volumio expects a JSON. Do you think that removing JSON validation would help. Do you know which string is sent?

To all the others reporting Volumio as non-free, where did you get this inaccurate info from? So we improve communication. Volumio is, and always be, FOSS. Just we have some premium features, which help tremendously in supporting the project, since you don't pay developers and staff with thin air.

@schnabel thanks for clarifying, sorry but I had to take a stance for what we believe in.

@eWuPi I agree that this would be the ideal situation, and it is possible to do it thanks to our new AAMPP framework:
https://developers.volumio.com/AAMPP/aampp-overview

The issue is that me and the whole dev team are super busy with fixing some quirks with the latest V3 release of Volumio, so it's not something we can find the time for at the moment.
But, if someone here wants to volunteer to develop such a plugin (or native integration) I will be glad to follow up closely and provide hints and make it happen.
